<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shu-Sin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 2037–2029 BCE</span> · Also known as Shu-Suen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shu-Sin was the fourth king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-dynasty-of-ur">Third Dynasty of Ur</a>, who reigned for about nine years in the late 21st century BCE. He campaigned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> and against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimashki-dynasty">Shimashki</a>, and built a long fortification wall, called 'Repeller of the Tidnum', to keep Amorite nomads out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumer">Sumer</a>. Like his predecessors he was worshipped as a god in his lifetime.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shu-sin.jpg" alt="Shu-Sin" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:5-mina_weight_Shu-Shin_Louvre_AO246.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
